      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{62b61f8ec938a62475e4cd14|full_name} \n\none of my worlds used this component heavily, `kinetic` (id: `wrld_b9a5532d-5c49-4938-88ff-2a1d948231cb`)\n\n`the bossa nova lounge` also used this extensively (id: `wrld_b8c7eb68-354a-4ec0-a9e4-68e88e2bcad9`)\n\nneither of these worlds exhibit the audio behavior that was initially noted pre-1768, and both of these worlds have not been updated as of build 1768. theoretically, they should still have these features enabled, but are audibly different now\n\nin `kinetic`'s case, i had made some bluesky posts showcasing an audio setup that used Steam Audio's `directionality` and `attenuation` in world, and that is part of my references to confirm the behavior has changed since then",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
