      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{61033e07b508635032c1e5ae|full_name}: I don't see anything special about these worlds. We never allowed these components to be used, and I don't see any way that they ever could have been in-use.\n\nWe publicly stated and documented multiple times that _no_ Steam Audio components are supported and you should _not_ install Steam Audio into world SDK projects. This is entirely unsupported.\n\nWhich build did you specifically see this working before? Do note that 1768 itself is the exact same build as 1767, the last beta build for Steam Audio. There were no changes whatsoever in that specific revision.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-12-04T21:52:55.347Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "during the Steam Audio Beta, world creators could use the official Steam Audio unitypackage in their worlds to enable `Directionality (Simulation Defined)` and `Attenuation (Curve Driven)`, allowing control over the \"width\" and \"vector\" of the audio (e.g. audio could be massively attenuated when the listener was behind the source)\n\nas of 2025.4.2, build 1768, this functionality is no longer present on existing and new uploads. please note this is not a report on the Steam Audio Component as a whole, there are features that are confirmed not to be implemented - this is a report on two specific features that were confirmed by the community to work prior to the release of Steam Audio",
  "error": null,
